Leave YAJSW's SIGAR out of the distribution.

SIGAR 1.6.4 (2010) is among YAJSW's optional extras for users' own
scripts. Its 64-bit Windows DLL truncates pointers: the first call,
Sigar.getPid(), reads 0xffffffffe67d7f88 and crashes the JVM, Temurin's as
well. Nothing in YAJSW or Ghidra's server configuration loads it; YAJSW's
manifests still name its jars, and Java skips class-path entries that do
not exist.

Upstream: not submitted
Applies-to: all environments

--- a/Ghidra/Features/GhidraServer/build.gradle
+++ b/Ghidra/Features/GhidraServer/build.gradle
@@ -50,6 +50,7 @@
 		include "${yajswRelease}/doc/**"
 		include "${yajswRelease}/LICENSE.txt"
 		include "${yajswRelease}/yajsw.policy.txt"
+		exclude "${yajswRelease}/lib/extended/sigar/**"
 	}
 }
 // Unpack YAJSW archive into build/data for development use
